WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
there are parts of Dark Souls II lore
that don't quite add up

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.120
unknown histories certain character
motivations origins of the curse and of

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.920
beings like the giants

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.190
these are unknown elements and that's
not really a bad thing

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:18.570
just like in Dark Souls 1 these unknown
elements will act as the gaps in the lore

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:23.519
we fill for ourselves in this video
though I want to question that lore my

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:27.720
best videos are based on interpretation
so before I do any interpreting I want

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.349
you to understand which parts of the lore 
currently don't have any concrete

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:36.420
answers I want you to know what topics
need answering when the DLC hits and I

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.969
want you to try and find answers for
yourselves

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:42.660
let's make it a bit more fun though
sometimes I'll engage in rampant

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.890
speculation and when I do this you'll
see this little button light up

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:51.360
For example: Did you know? That Gavlan's wheel
and deal quote is in reference to how he

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.170
wheels Darkdiver Grandahl all around to
get two different locations so that he

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:59.699
can pay for his crippling alcohol
addiction to Heineken? You can find

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:01.890
shortcuts to topics in the description.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.369
We have four major topics: And the first
one we're going to talk about is the

00:01:05.369 --> 00:01:06.540
opening cutscene

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.020
so, in this cutscene we have to answer
four questions:

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:15.750
Who are we? Where are we? Who is the woman?
and most importantly: When are we?

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.970
The most obvious question and answer is:
Who we are: We are a wandering Undead

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.320
it seems as if we've lost our memory of
our past, life based on the dialogue and

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.480
the fact that these two are melting away.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.130
The second question: Where are we in the
cutscene? At the start I actually think

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.479
that it's irrelevant.

00:01:33.479 --> 00:01:37.680
We're just a wanderer who comes upon
this old woman, but it becomes relevant

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.119
when we come upon the ruins of Drangleic and considering these ruins

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:46.530
I think what's most important is when we
are. The old lady tells us that one day

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:51.240
we're going to stand upon the decrepit
gate of Drangleic without really knowing why.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.329
This puts our actions in Drangelic in
the past.

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:58.530
So when we arrive at this portal we are
traveling to a kingdom that existed a

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.770
long time ago

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:03.399
and that's where the entire game takes
place so that's significant.

00:02:03.399 --> 00:02:08.500
So the next question: Who is this old
lady to lay this prophecy upon us?

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.940
Well there is a fourth firekeeper
mentioned in the firekeeper hut.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.880
A firekeeper who left the others a fair time
ago.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.800
I believe this cinematic old lady is the
fourth firekeeper and that's for a few reasons:

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.420
For one she's wearing the red firekeeper garb,
but what's really interesting is that we

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.760
have a lot of evidence that she's an
aged emerald Herald:

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.470
Firstly in the credits we're told that
there is a young and an old version of Shanalotte;

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.819
Secondly she has very similar dialogue
to the Herald at the Dragon Aerie

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:40.220
When she says that we shall walk those
grounds without really knowing why.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.240
And lastly the Herald mentions that it
was her own manifestation that led us to Drangleic.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:50.019
The Emerald Harold is also
called Firekeeper in game by Navlaan;

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.440
The guardian of the Far fire the fourth
Firekeeper.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.720
The connection between the Herald and the aged woman

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:00.280
has also been confirmed by people who are working on the official guide.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.640
So now that we know that the woman is an
aged version of the Emerald Herald

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:09.060
we have our first question: Why is she
laying this prophecy upon us?

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:13.930
Why is she sending us back? The old woman in the hut says:  You spoke to that kind

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.100
old dear didn't you?

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:19.329
You're finished. Implying that they know
what the Emerald Herald is trying to do.

00:03:19.329 --> 00:03:23.799
The dialogue also reminds us that
they've seen other undead passed through here.

00:03:23.799 --> 00:03:28.599
All who have shared the same fate: Hollowing.
They have this air of disdain for what

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.220
the Emerald Herald or the fourth
Firekeeper seems to be trying to do

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:36.970
Their sister seems to be sending undead
back to Drangleic through this limbo

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:40.900
called Things Betwixt perhaps in some
effort to alter the past.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:46.000
So what past needs to be altered? If you
watched my video on the ending you might know

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.020
Our character's goal in this game is to link the fire.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.060
The young Emerald Herald's goal is to get us to link the fire

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:56.440
The Emerald Herald tiredly guides the undead who come through Majula

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.560
Undead who appear to have been sent from the future.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:07.430
I've always thought that the Emerald
Herald's dialogue sounded really tired and weary and if she's had to guide
hundreds and hundreds of undead along

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.910
the same path to their hallowed fate
then I could explain why

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:15.200
in fact this whole thing is actually
somewhat reminiscent of how our

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.340
character in Dark Souls 1 is sent back
in order to stop the spread of the Abyss

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.360
with Manus

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.530
Think about it: The entire game of Dark
Souls 2 is about the cycles. Things that

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.280
happened in the first game in Lordran
happen again in Drangleic. The

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.920
framework is the same but the players
change.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:35.000
So just like in Dark Souls 1 when we were
sent back to Oolacile to stop Manus

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:35.750
his abyss

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:39.800
we're being sent back to Drangleic in
order to stop nashandra spreading her

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.320
own abyss and that's my theory anyway

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.520
speaking of cycles though a lot of you
don't like the idea of cycles and that's

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:47.330
okay

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:51.200
do bear in mind though that these are
concepts much more accepted in eastern

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.360
mythologies than in Western ones

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:56.990
it really drives through that
hopelessness of what we're doing but if

00:04:56.990 --> 00:05:01.400
we are to see a dark souls 3 then I hope
it deals with our breaking of the cycle

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.880
somehow because if we just get another
cycle in Dark Souls 3 that would be

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.200
pretty disappointing

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.560
so there wasn't too much rampant
speculation on the discussion of this

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.310
opening

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.570
I think a lot of this speculation can be
fairly valid if you find any loopholes

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.310
in my theories then let me know

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:20.750
let's move on to something you can help
me with though the Giants. We'll start

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.550
with the facts what we know.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.850
Long ago the Queen came to King Vendrick
alone from a faraway land

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:30.320
she warned him of a looming threat
across the seas the Giants.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.940
It's not said whether they actually were
a threat or not but the King crossed the

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:39.800
ocean defeated the Giants pillaged their
land and brought back a prize.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:44.180
So two questions come up with this topic:
Who are the giants and what was stolen

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:47.180
from them? And we don't have definite
answers to these questions.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.960
It's an example of a really major
missing plot point in the game

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.370
ultimately I think this might be
revealed in some sort of dlc but there

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.880
are a few ideas floating around
currently about who the Giants are so

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:02.330
I'll clue you in on some of my favorite
ones and i'll let you make your own

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:07.130
decisions in terms of a timeline we know
that the Giants appeared after nashandra

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:11.180
came to vendrick she came from a far-off
land and warned him of the Giants

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:14.249
calling them a looming threat from
across the seas

00:06:14.249 --> 00:06:18.539
my interpretation is that she used this
information to get closer to vendrick

00:06:18.539 --> 00:06:23.789
giving him apparently vital information
and conveniently placing her close to

00:06:23.789 --> 00:06:26.249
the throne. Were they actually a threat?

00:06:26.249 --> 00:06:30.419
Probably not. Captain Drummond calls the
invasion of the Giants misguided

00:06:30.419 --> 00:06:34.829
barbarism and I'm inclined to believe it
if I had to draw parallels to Dark

00:06:34.829 --> 00:06:39.449
Souls 1 i'd say it's similar to how
Gwyn engaged the ancient dragons

00:06:39.449 --> 00:06:43.979
so who are these giants honestly. I'm
just inclined to believe that the giants

00:06:43.979 --> 00:06:48.029
are an entirely new entry to the soul
series since there isn't really much

00:06:48.029 --> 00:06:51.479
evidence that they've existed in some
other form in Dark Souls 1

00:06:52.049 --> 00:06:56.819
One theory I do kind of like calls them
a reincarnation of dragons

00:06:56.819 --> 00:07:00.779
the ancient dragon drops a giant soul
after all and while everyone assumes

00:07:00.779 --> 00:07:04.860
that the giant soul was a part of the
dragon due to experimentation with Aldia

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:08.789
what if the devs wanted us to come to
the conclusion that the dragon was a

00:07:08.789 --> 00:07:12.599
giant. This is further emphasized when
you consider the plaque on the back of

00:07:12.599 --> 00:07:17.549
the Majula obelisk. It's cut content
but it says that the Giants crossed the

00:07:17.549 --> 00:07:19.739
Seas perhaps to return home.

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:23.729
So are they coming home to Drangleic
Since Drangleic is touted as being

00:07:23.729 --> 00:07:27.809
Lordran who's to say that the dragons
aren't coming back in some other form?

00:07:27.809 --> 00:07:33.299
the only other link i have to them being
the same being as dragons is that Giants

00:07:33.299 --> 00:07:37.709
grow into trees and these trees could be
the arch trees of the dragons in some

00:07:37.709 --> 00:07:41.699
sort of long evolutionary cycle but this
is a long shot.

00:07:41.699 --> 00:07:46.409
Also in reference to the plaque it could
be talking about how the Giants left

00:07:46.409 --> 00:07:47.639
Drangleic

00:07:47.639 --> 00:07:52.139
not necessarily that they came to Drangleic. All it says is that they returned

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:52.589
home.

00:07:52.589 --> 00:07:56.759
So since the obelisk is a war monument I
guess it kind of makes sense that

00:07:56.759 --> 00:08:00.719
they're commemorating the fact that the
Giants left. That they retreated

00:08:00.719 --> 00:08:05.610
you know. Anyway other theories say that
they are the Lords from Lordran that

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:10.129
perhaps this is the withered form they
could take once they lose their souls

00:08:10.129 --> 00:08:14.060
a few people notice that the giant Lords
outfit looked a lot like Gwyn's.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:17.980
It doesn't really explain why they grow
into trees though so i wouldn't say that

00:08:17.989 --> 00:08:21.949
they're the same race and if Drangleic
is Lordran why would the Giants be

00:08:21.949 --> 00:08:22.669
elsewhere

00:08:22.669 --> 00:08:26.449
so as much as I'd love an explanation of
what the Giants are

00:08:26.449 --> 00:08:30.139
it doesn't look like we have a solid
theory just yet. Moving on

00:08:30.139 --> 00:08:32.930
Vendrick brought a
prize back from the Giants when he

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:36.409
invaded and there's a lot of speculation
regarding what this could have been

00:08:37.009 --> 00:08:41.930
whatever it was it has to be related to
the Vendrick's ability to create golems

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:46.519
since Drummond directly states that he
brought back a prize and then the golems

00:08:46.519 --> 00:08:47.839
materialized.

00:08:47.839 --> 00:08:51.649
So some say it's the Lord vessel which
is cracked in the basement of the

00:08:51.649 --> 00:08:52.970
Majula mansion

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:57.079
the Lord vessel holds souls and studying
it could have given Vendrick the ability

00:08:57.079 --> 00:09:01.759
to place souls into inanimate objects
and other common reasoning is that this

00:09:01.759 --> 00:09:05.750
would explain all the Lord souls from
dark souls 1 being present in dark souls

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:10.519
2 though this is problematic reasoning
for a few reasons one it's already been

00:09:10.519 --> 00:09:14.300
fairly established that Drangleic is a
reincarnation of Lordran

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.449
so why would the Lord vessel be overseas
in the first place

00:09:17.449 --> 00:09:20.899
and two we know that vendrick had
already risen to power and defeated the

00:09:20.899 --> 00:09:23.600
four old ones by the time he attacked
the Giants

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.439
so it's unlikely that it's the Lord
vessel. Some say it's the Ashen Mist

00:09:27.439 --> 00:09:30.829
Heart which allows you to delve into the
memories of the withered

00:09:30.829 --> 00:09:33.560
this could explain how Vendrick and Aldia peered into

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:37.189
the very essence of the soul though it
doesn't really explain how they

00:09:37.189 --> 00:09:41.839
developed the ability to create golems
and some say it's the throne of want

00:09:41.839 --> 00:09:42.680
itself

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:46.459
I don't like any of these suggestions
but i like this theory the most for a

00:09:46.459 --> 00:09:47.569
few reasons

00:09:47.569 --> 00:09:52.279
a) the throne seems built for a much
taller being. b) you need the Giants'

00:09:52.279 --> 00:09:56.959
kinship for the doors to even open. A
kinship means to be blood-related or to

00:09:56.959 --> 00:10:01.970
share characteristics or origins. And c)
Nashandra implies that she wants

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:05.810
access when she bitterly remarks that
vendrick never sat the true throne

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:09.670
so it could have been the motivation for
her to invade the giants in the first

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.420
place

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:14.770
and d) the throne is surrounded by
golems that only react to the Giants'

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:15.790
kinship.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:19.000
I don't think any of these opinions are
definitively true or false

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:22.960
I think the intention of the developers
was that you were never supposed to know

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:27.160
quite what vendrick stole and this is
what makes Nashandra's intention so

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:30.790
vague and it's what makes the Giants'
intentions so alien

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:34.360
and once we figure this out I feel like
many other aspects of the game will fall

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.350
into place

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:39.130
speaking of Nashandra though there's a
fair bit that doesn't quite add up with

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:43.120
her so Nashandra is well known to be a
fragment of Manus at this point

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:47.740
she also looks a lot like dusk who Manus
both steals and releases in Dark Souls 1

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:50.380
DLC if we follow this reasoning

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:55.089
while we're on the topic of dusk we can
assume that a) dusk is nashandra and is

00:10:55.089 --> 00:10:57.910
more than just a damsel in distress in
the first game

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:02.620
her name is dusk after all which means
to grow dark. Or b) the fragment of

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:06.760
Manus that develops into nashandra
simply gets an impression of dusk or c)

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:10.150
the fragment infects dusk and grows
within her

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:12.940
they're all possible and they're all
interesting I really like to think that

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:16.870
there's more going on with dusk
since her name seems to imply a little

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:21.250
bit more. When we meet nashandra she's
sitting on the simple throne alone no

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:25.390
one quite seems to know where vendrick
is but her with Wellager saying the

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:26.920
Queen has taken him

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:30.490
that must be what it looks like to Wellager. The Queen tells you to visit

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:34.900
vendrick then when he's dead proclaims
that Drangleic is no longer

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:38.589
she then tells you to seek the throne
and do what needs to be done

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:42.760
so she's guiding you in the right
direction she's guiding you to the

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:43.330
throne

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:46.360
aka the kiln in order to link the fire

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:49.720
so why is she doing this. She says it's
what must be done

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:53.020
so it's almost like she's given up
almost like she knows what's going to

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:57.040
happen and if the popular theory is
right there isn't much that she can do

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.750
before vendrick died he locked half the
kingdom away behind sealed gates only he

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:06.100
could open and then he shut himself away
so deeply in the crypt that nashandra

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.000
couldn't easily follow

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:12.230
so we get to the end of the game and we
fight nashandra she tells us how we've

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:15.470
proven ourselves to her and how we will
become one with the dark

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:19.970
her intentions are still vague the only
conclusion that i can come to is that

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:21.590
she led us to the throne

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:24.770
knowing that we were the only one who
could get that far

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:30.260
since she couldn't she then plans to usurp us at the last second and ascend

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:31.850
the throne for herself

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:35.270
the official guide says that she's found
